<%!-- [LEGAL REVIEW] Draft terms, to be reviewed by a lawyer before launch.
     Placeholders in [BRACKETS] must be filled in. The "What you upload"
     section is what sign-up, guest uploads and music uploads ask people to
     agree to: if its meaning changes, bump Accounts.terms_version/0 so
     everyone is asked again. --%>
<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope} shell={:marketing}>
  <article
    id="terms"
    class="mx-auto flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-7 px-4 py-14 text-[15px] leading-relaxed sm:px-8"
  >
    <header class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="text-ks-muted">Version {@version}</p>
      <p
        id="terms-review-note"
        class="rounded-box border border-accent/40 bg-ks-amber-soft px-4 py-3 text-sm text-ks-amber-deep"
      >
        [LEGAL REVIEW] These terms are a working draft and will be reviewed before launch.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section id="terms-service" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">1. Who we are and what this covers</h2>
      <p>
        Keepsake is run by [COMPANY NAME], [ADDRESS] ("we"). These terms cover your use of Keepsake:
        the website, your account, and the albums you create and share. By creating an account, or by
        adding photos to someone's album as a guest, you agree to them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-account" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">2. Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You need to be at least [MINIMUM AGE] to create an account. Keep your password safe and your
        email address current; you're responsible for what happens under your account. You can turn on
        two-step login in Settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-uploads" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">3. What you upload</h2>
      <p>
        You keep ownership of the photos, music and words you add. You must own them, or have
        permission from whoever does, to upload and share them. That includes music you add to a
        slideshow: you are responsible for having the rights to use it, and for any claim that you didn't.
      </p>
      <p>
        Guests who add photos to an album confirm the same for the photos they add. The album's owner
        decides what is shown.
      </p>
      <p>
        You give us permission to store, resize and show your content only to run the service for you
        and the people you share with. We don't sell it, and we don't use it for advertising.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-sharing" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">4. Sharing, guests and collaborators</h2>
      <p>
        Anyone with an album's link and access code can see it. Keep codes to the people you mean to
        share with, and change the code if it spreads further. People you invite as collaborators can add
        and edit photos (editors) or see every photo (viewers); you can remove them at any time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-payments" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">5. Plans, trials and payments</h2>
      <p>
        New accounts start on a free trial. When it ends you can choose a paid plan or continue on the
        Free plan; nothing you've added is deleted, but you can't add more than Free allows. Paid plans
        are billed monthly or yearly by card through Flutterwave, renew automatically, and can be
        cancelled any time in Settings (you keep the plan until the period ends). Refunds are at our
        discretion unless the law requires otherwise. [LEGAL REVIEW: refund policy]
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-removal" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">6. Content and accounts we may remove</h2>
      <p>
        Don't use Keepsake for anything illegal, for content that exploits or harms anyone, or for content
        you don't have the rights to. We may remove content, or pause an account, when we receive a
        credible report that it breaks these terms or the law. Anyone can report an album from its page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-ending" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">7. Leaving</h2>
      <p>
        You can export everything and delete your account at any time from Settings. Deletion takes
        effect after 14 days, during which you can change your mind; invoices are kept for our accounting.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-liability" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">8. Our responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        We work hard to keep Keepsake running and your photos safe, and we keep backups, but we can't
        promise the service will never be interrupted. Please keep your own copies of photos that matter.
        [LEGAL REVIEW: limitation of liability, governing law ([JURISDICTION]) and disputes]
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-changes" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">9. Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        If we change these terms in a way that matters, we'll tell you by email or in the app before the
        change applies. Questions: [CONTACT EMAIL]. How we handle personal data is in our <.link
          href={~p"/privacy"}
          class="font-medium underline"
        >Privacy notice</.link>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layouts.app>
